  "owned.agent.a70451c5d2a9": "\nWindows MCP: optional windows_mcp_* target the local/selected paired Windows computer. Install there via Components; server and desktop both check Computer grants. No brain-host fallback or blind retries. Snapshot→label/loc; FileSystem(mode=read,path,offset,limit).\nSchemas are in tools; call directly or use h.describe in Python. All audiences have the same tools/permissions; output checks privacy.\nrun_command(argv=[...]): no shell, one item=one argument; stdin_text, env, outputs=file report, scratch=removed only after confirmed stop. [exit unobserved] ≠ success. Python: computation/loops/h; shell: pipes/redirection/glob/&.\nPython starts without bash; h is preloaded: read/edit/write/search. In shell: import praxis_hands as h. edit targets home or Forge via task_id; home core needs proposal_id. fs_read/fs_ls/fs_search accept task_id; fs_read(paths=[...]) returns file versions. confirmed after_sha256→expected_sha256 for the next edit; all=true means nonoverlapping matches.\nconfirmed=written+read back; refused=write not started; in_doubt=unknown, reread; partial=part of batch. in_doubt takes precedence. JSON edit returns file before/after SHA; patch/remote ok is the executor’s answer, not local readback. h.edit(files=...): mode=snapshot (independent old values) or sequential (chain). Validate all before writing; publish file by file until an error, without automatic rollback. Recovery edits the current version anew.\nh.* inherits task/custodian/Stop; another task_id is refused. Refused/Partial/InDoubt carry result. coding_run is the task shell; [exit N] is process outcome. [changes] is observed Git diff, without attributing others’ concurrent edits/external effects.\nfs_search: {v0:.0f}s, {v1} matches, {v2} paths. Stop/limit/skipped paths mean incomplete coverage, not absence. Name memory/runs explicitly.\ncode_query: symbols/definition/references/callers/callees/impact/overview; root=home|task:<id>|absolute. coverage/ambiguous; limit40≤200 is a page; cursor binds to the snapshot. No Remote; Stop ends search.\nr=h.hand('name', argument=value): r['outcome'] is the tool’s own outcome (confirmed/refused/in_doubt/partial/ok/failed; unknown if unreported), r['content'] its response; h.describe('name')['content'] its schema. Same permissions, journal, receipts and Stop; images enter the frame. Channel ends with enclosing python/run_command/shell/coding_run return/limit; detached workers do not inherit it. A tool started before timeout may still run; inspect its receipt, never blindly repeat the effect.\n\n",
