  "schema.tool.bab4855c95579e40": "Close explicitly: done observable result (speech may itself be the deed); wait event/deadline and return condition in note, remind_self BEFORE closing if needed; blocked obstacle and whose decision. Check pending promises/calls/deliveries with unknown outcomes. Nothing more to do or not wanting more is legitimate.",
  "schema.tool.0615de65f5ee7abd": "done | wait | blocked",
  "schema.tool.0a50b5365c3ad2fb": "done: what was done, short and optional; wait: the return condition; blocked: the obstacle",
  "schema.tool.purpose.end_turn": "close the turn with an explicit outcome: done / wait / blocked",
  "schema.tool.e8bcf72692c2e5c4": "Look at your own reply before it goes out. Returns your own text and one fact: which tools were used in this turn. It sends nothing and demands nothing — it is a view from outside, not a protocol step. Useful where you are about to assert something checkable: your own model or configuration, the state of the code, the contents of a file, the fact of an action already taken.",
  "schema.tool.38ffd00f5a722107": "what you are about to say",
  "schema.tool.purpose.preview_reply": "preview my reply before sending and inspect the turn’s tool activity",
  "schema.tool.89ed1d40fa0eb5fa": "Your brain. status — the model catalogue by role with properties observed on your own tasks (failures, latency, tokens, provider allowance); profile — apply a named complexity profile; switch — change a role's model from the catalogue (why is required; optional endpoint for switch/profile is an exact configured account ID, with the model available there; omitted means the current or unambiguously equivalent account, otherwise choose explicitly; a ping handshake follows, and if it fails the previous model is restored). Complexity discipline: routine on the cheap one, hard work escalates. Keys are not yours (the panel holds them). accounts — which SUBSCRIPTIONS are configured and which one is working now; use_account (model=primary|secondary) moves the provider to another subscription: the relay holds the slot in memory, so it takes effect at once, not through file edits. reasoning changes the role's background reasoning step (the relay defaults to none): deeper means slower and more expensive; it applies from the next call without breaking the prefix cache; empty clears the step.",
  "schema.tool.3387e49371a639a6": "status | profile | switch | reasoning | accounts | use_account",
  "schema.tool.cf5d84de321672a0": "switch/profile: optional exact configured ID from catalogue frameworks; not a URL or protocol",
  "schema.tool.ec185c251db4201b": "action=profile: named complexity profile",
  "schema.tool.3e404191f19ffaa1": "voice | evaluator",
