  "native.shell.windows": "Local shell on this Windows computer: bash -lc through the bundled busybox. This is not Linux/WSL: the name bash in PowerShell/cmd may resolve to WSL, while this tool uses the bundled interpreter. busybox may call an elevated account root; that name alone does not establish Linux. PowerShell: powershell.exe -NoProfile -Command …; cmd: cmd.exe /d /c …; the computer tool is also available if enabled. Home: {home}; soul: {home}/soul (SOUL.md, self/CURRENT.md, skills/); memory: {home}/memory; working files: {home}/workspace. Code: {code}; application: {app}. Default cwd: {cwd}; if the configured folder disappears, home is used. Use full paths with forward slashes. Access follows the current fence and OS permissions, not this description. Default timeout {timeout} s, maximum 600 s. Read the final status/receipt; a lost response or timeout does not prove process-tree termination. One program without a shell pipeline: run_command(argv=[...]). Change code through edit or praxis_hands with version and write-ownership checks.",
  "native.shell.posix": "Local shell on this computer ({system}): bash -lc. Home: {home}; soul: {home}/soul (SOUL.md, self/CURRENT.md, skills/); memory: {home}/memory; working files: {home}/workspace. Code: {code}; application: {app}. Default cwd: {cwd}; if the configured folder disappears, home is used. Use full paths. Access follows the current fence and OS permissions, not this description. Default timeout {timeout} s, maximum 600 s. Read the final status/receipt; a lost response or timeout does not prove process-tree termination. One program without a shell pipeline: run_command(argv=[...]). Change code through edit or praxis_hands with version and write-ownership checks.",
  "native.shell.command": "Shell command for bash -lc; the command content is passed literally.",
  "native.shell.cwd": "Folder to run in. Default {cwd}; a relative path is resolved from {home}.",
  "native.shell.timeout": "Time limit in seconds: default {timeout}, maximum 600.",
  "native.shell.purpose": "Local bash on {system}; cwd {cwd}. Current state determines permissions/isolation; code writes use edit/praxis_hands.",
  "native.schema.mount.0": "Ask the owner for access to a folder outside the Hélène home in isolated mode. ask: full path, a short why for the owner, access=read|write. list: mounted folders, pending requests and refusals. A request does not open a folder: the owner decides. Repeating it does not bypass a recorded refusal.",
  "native.schema.mount.1": "ask: request a folder; list: access and request inventory.",
  "native.schema.mount.2": "Full folder path.",
  "native.schema.mount.3": "Why the folder is needed, one line for the owner.",
  "native.schema.mount.4": "read: read only; write: read and write.",
  "native.schema.mount.purpose": "Request folder access in isolated mode; the owner grants access.",
  "native.schema.self_review.0": "Voluntary independent Forge review: choose the question, criteria, materials and depth when criticism helps. Ordinary work may finish without review or a skip ritual. Omit subject for legacy source-only review; otherwise freeze a typed plan (text), change (matching base/candidate material refs and explicit absences), or task_result (assignment, exact answer, artifacts, effect/check claims). Existing materials require exact SHA; materials stay owner-only, without ambient memory access or execution. Update conflicts use source_update and its mandatory verification panel, not ordinary disposition. Verdicts and author decisions stay separate; clear source/materials do not prove installed behavior. Owner dialogue only.",
  "native.schema.self_review.1": "Ordinary request: 1..8 critics using existing configured voice models; default follows policy/depth.",
  "native.schema.self_review.2": "plan: exact authored plan text.",
  "native.schema.self_review.3": "task_result: original assignment.",
  "native.schema.self_review.4": "task_result: exact answer, never a summary substituted later.",
  "native.schema.self_review.5": "Author claims, not host attestations.",
  "native.schema.self_review.6": "Author claims; attach exact evidence as materials.",
  "native.schema.self_review.7": "Logical name, identical on both change sides.",
  "native.schema.self_review.8": "Explicit relative UTF-8 file path; no memory, configuration, credentials or links.",
  "native.schema.self_review.9": "SHA of exact bytes; omit SHA for absent material.",
  "native.schema.self_review.purpose": "Voluntary independent review of a plan, change or result; verdict and author decision stay separate.",
  "native.schema.kit.0": "Review a distribution proposal to my SOUL/VOICE/self/skill Markdown. list shows IDs; read returns complete proposed and previous text. reject records refusal. accept only acknowledges bytes I have already written through manage_identity/write_skill, or fs_write with CAS for INDEX. This tool never edits my soul.",
  "native.schema.kit.purpose": "Review a distribution persona/skill proposal; accept only your own already-written revision.",
  "native.schema.inspection.0": "Inspect an installed update. status shows the request, release goals and reported bugs. report saves your factual findings: passed/problem/unverified and verifiable evidence for each item. Unchecked means unverified with a reason. After report, tell the owner the result through reply. This tool neither accepts installation nor enables rollback.",
  "native.schema.inspection.purpose": "Record factual installed-update checks, including unverified items.",
  "native.schema.source_update.0": "Resolve one complete owner-requested update. status lists selected_cores: core-0/path and core-1/path address distinct cores; app/path is the one shared application. diff shows A->local and A->incoming; read paginates one side. resolve supplies full UTF-8 text or a side; patch replaces an exact before/after fragment. Repairs outside conflicts need reason and expected_candidate_sha256 from status. finish declares the semantic candidate complete. For new automatic jobs, the durable updater then runs composition-bound selected/full verification, independent review and the already-authorized mechanical switch after clear. Read status, repair actual findings and finish again; do not restart the same work or ask for fresh permission. verify records exact scope; widen it with full_tests or extra_tests and test_reason on finish/verify. Review requires exact evidence, not merely passing tests; apply requires clear review. Acceptance is delegated to you: inspect panel evidence, repair findings and verify installed behavior after the authorized update. Do not ask the owner to run or reconfirm review. status supplies candidate_state, review_evidence and next_action. Run the relevant user journey yourself, including available headless UI checks. Check offered tool/input, actual harness execution and returned model observation separately. A request does not prove execution; source tests do not prove installed acceptance. Use this update panel, not ordinary self_review on the old live Forge. Clear binds exact source bytes; never manufacture approval or bypass Stop.",
  "native.schema.source_update.1": "Widen verification to the full battery; requires test_reason.",
  "native.schema.source_update.2": "Additional exact test-module paths; requires test_reason.",
  "native.schema.source_update.3": "Why dynamic or indirect impact requires these additional checks.",
  "native.schema.source_update.purpose": "Isolated update candidate: conflict resolution, exact verification, independent review and authorized installation.",
  "native.schema.update_server.0": "Update Hélène on this server through its external executor; do not replace your own container from inside. The executor verifies the official release, version, archive and sha256; with owner consent it downloads/builds the update, keeps a copy and carries over tree/ and app/ edits. Unmerged edits remain in workspace/update-<version>/. You stop briefly, then receive a new-version notice. Inspect the result and report problems; installation does not wait for your acceptance. Explain versions and changes plainly, leaving technical details for when asked. status: executor availability, installed/new version and latest plan. plan: version=number or latest; backup=full (code and all data/, default) or code (without a data/ copy when space is limited); a brief reason for the owner. If the owner directly requests this update or agrees to this proposal, pass their exact words in owner_words: updating starts immediately. Otherwise the plan waits for consent by button or words. confirm: confirm an existing pending plan only in an owner-originated turn and only with their consent to that exact plan; owner_words must be verbatim. Do not decide for them. decline removes a pending plan with reason. Inspect the application and your edits after updating. There is no deadline acceptance or rollback by silence; report problems in an ordinary message.",
  "native.schema.update_server.1": "status | plan | confirm | decline",
  "native.schema.update_server.2": "For plan: a version number or latest by default.",
  "native.schema.update_server.3": "For plan: full by default, or code.",
  "native.schema.update_server.4": "For plan/decline: a brief reason the owner will read.",
  "native.schema.update_server.5": "The owner’s verbatim consent to this update/plan; never invent it.",
  "native.schema.update_server.purpose": "Server update through the external executor with owner consent.",
  "native.schema.update_desktop.0": "Update Hélène on this computer. status reads state; plan proposes a release (version: latest or a number). An ordinary Python update preserves authored code edits and merges them with the release; memory, conversations, settings and pause are preserved. Clean replacement requires explicit source_mode=clean. Pass exact owner_words from the direct request; an authorized update needs no repeated consent. confirm/decline decide a proposal. Resolve conflicts only in the current isolated candidate through source_update: status, diff, patch, finish. The incoming executor handles exact-candidate checks and independent review; observe their results and repair findings. Ordinary self_review is no substitute; do not create personal reminders. The updater installs, restarts and restores after failure. Verify the result after restart; do not replace the program through other tools outside the job. A direct update request is work to completion: find the stage, take available steps and continue after worker results. A promise is insufficient; do not await another Update click or renewed consent for authorized acceptance. Use a verified release and exact candidate with retained edits. Installation does not wait for your acceptance or roll back by silence. If the path breaks, establish the concrete cause and continuation, preserve results and report the obstacle; endless alarms are no substitute. Respect Stop/Pause, cancellation and tool boundaries.",
  "native.schema.update_desktop.purpose": "Authorized desktop update: preserve edits, complete the conflict panel and verify installed results.",
  "native.schema.appearance.0": "Read or change this installation’s appearance. Read first; patch/reset require seen. patch is an array of {{key,value}} entries containing only keys to change; value is a string (JSON for helene.look) or explicit null to delete. Look: uiScale 0.7..1.5; style paper/clean/studio/glass/terminal; font hand/sans/serif/mono; shape default/round/square; backdrop plain/grid/glow; density comfortable/compact; dayColor/nightColor/accentColor in hex. frame.theme system/light/dark; frame.rail/panel: 0 shown, 1 collapsed; widths 220..700. Never changes agent identity or configuration.",
  "native.schema.appearance.purpose": "Installation appearance: read first, then patch/reset with current seen.",
  "schema.tool.7a311a1aca572342": "Run Python directly without shell quoting. h already contains praxis_hands: h.read, h.edit, h.write, h.search use the same editor, version checks and receipts. h.hand(\"name\", **args) calls a tool in this turn’s authorized catalogue through the live parent dispatcher, with its rights, durable receipts and Stop. r[\"outcome\"] is the tool’s own outcome (confirmed/refused/in_doubt/partial/ok/failed; unknown if absent); print r[\"content\"] for its reply. It also has result_ref, call_id and image_count. h.describe(\"name\")[\"content\"] gives the full schema. InDoubt means inspect the receipt, never blindly repeat an effect. The bridge expires when the outer call returns or reaches its ceiling; an already-started nested tool may finish after the script stops waiting, with its receipt after [exit N]. Standalone/background survivors have no live bridge. Print needed results. cwd defaults to the configured home working directory, or the local Forge task root with task_id. Local tasks inherit process custody and Stop; remote tasks are refused before execution. At home timeout=0 uses the configured shell default (normally 30 s), capped at 600 s; in a task 0 means no deadline. Read [exit N] and tree-stop facts: leader exit, a lost reply or timeout alone do not prove descendant termination. Prefer h.edit to whole-file string replacement. For one program with exact arguments use run_command.",
  "schema.tool.12c56aba2a3f2ec6": "Python source, exact line numbers preserved; h is preloaded",
  "schema.tool.88a9be0c56896484": "Working directory; task paths are relative to the task root",
  "schema.tool.d40ae21d428bb4b1": "Seconds; 0 uses home default or no task deadline",
  "schema.tool.aa00ba579506588b": "Optional local Forge task; omitted means home",
  "schema.tool.purpose.python": "execute Python with preloaded h and the authorized tool bridge",
  "schema.tool.0054ff5a6a0abdb3": "Run one program with exact arguments and no shell: argv[0] is a PATH name or path relative to cwd; each other item reaches it as one argument. Quotes, spaces, ;, $(), *, ~, backslashes and newlines are literal data, never expanded. Use this for ordinary program calls (git show, pytest, ffmpeg); python for computation, loops or h; shell only for its grammar (pipes, redirects, globs, &&, background &). It never falls back to shell. Routes: local home with the configured cwd and the same execution boundary as shell; or a local Forge task with task_id, its root, admission, custody, Stop and full log. Remote host/Windows backends accepting only shell strings are refused before sending; use coding_run or an available computer tool there. At home timeout=0 uses the configured default (normally 30 s), capped at 600 s; in a task it means no deadline. stdin_text is sent exactly as UTF-8 then EOF; omitted means closed stdin. stdout/stderr are combined; full output is retained. The reply ends with a [run_command {{...}}] facts line (executor, cwd, argv, resolved program, exit_code/signal, timed_out and tree_stop), [changes] and [exit N]. [exit unobserved] means no exit status was observed, never success. refused means nothing launched (bad argv, missing program/cwd); in_doubt means it may have run: check before repeating. Non-zero exit does not mean nothing changed. See env, outputs and scratch fields; they also appear in the facts.",
  "schema.tool.3d6b3d07702e36ff": "Program then its arguments, one array item per argument",
  "schema.tool.69ed0f87ef1a25d2": "Working directory; configured home cwd by default, task paths relative to the task root.",
