  "schema.tool.purpose.run_command": "run a program with exact argv, without a shell",
  "schema.tool.46637750b119f7c9": "Read-only code evidence in home, a local Forge task, or an absolute external tree; never creates a task/project or a write right. Python AST definitions, calls, references and import bindings; unknown receivers and shadowing stay ambiguous, never proven edges. JS/TS use disclosed regex symbols and text mentions; no LSP/type or re-export resolution. Returns snapshot, rows, total, next_cursor, coverage and methods. Empty incomplete scans do not prove absence. line is 1-based, char Unicode code points, byte UTF-8 column; end exclusive, CRLF excluded. Page limit is independent of the named Forge scan budget (normally 12000 files/90 seconds). Cursor binds query and file hashes: changed files refuse with paths; restart expires parent-held cursors. Structural cache is disposable and stores no snippets/source/literals; external roots use process RAM only. Heavy work uses the run-owned search process and stops with run reset. Remote host/Windows tasks are explicitly unsupported. impact is heuristic; its verification_plan(full=True) remains the full gate, overview is factual inventory.",
