  "schema.tool.f810778ab492c1d2": "Local bash shell at home with the configured working directory; if a temporary directory disappears, home is used. Use full paths and the current installation’s actual capabilities. Use shell for its grammar: pipes, redirects, globs and &&. One program with exact arguments: run_command(argv=[...]); computation and loops: python. Edit code through edit or praxis_hands (h.read/h.edit/h.write/h.search), with version and write-ownership checks: shell itself does not hold the shared mutation lock. cwd selects the folder; timeout selects the limit, 0 uses the configured default (normally 30 s), maximum 600 s. Read [exit N] and stop facts; non-zero means failure, and a lost reply or timeout does not prove descendant termination. Do not replace versioned editing with whole-file str.replace.",
