  "schema.tool.3b31b92bd5f91bda": "Pin a single-file page to its full SHA; changed bytes refuse.",
  "schema.tool.purpose.fs_read": "read a file or batch with SHA and pagination",
  "schema.tool.63a2ceb431eaf646": "YOUR EDITING HAND. Without task_id, paths are in your home: workspace/soul/memory; core edits need proposal_id. With task_id, paths and execution belong to that Forge task. replace: old occurs exactly once, or all=true replaces all non-overlapping matches; write: full content (home overwrite/force are explicit); patch: unified diff in a Forge task, git apply --check then apply, no per-file SHA guarantee; batch: versioned replacements. Pass expected_sha256 from fs_read; a confirmed edit after_sha256 is valid for the next edit. Reply is edit: JSON, status/message/before_sha256/after_sha256 and files for a batch. confirmed means written and read back; refused means untouched; in_doubt means outcome unknown: reread, NEVER retry blind. Patch success is ok, not readback-confirmed. Remote success is ok (backend-reported, no local readback promise); ambiguous errors/lost replies are in_doubt. Shell does not hold the shared mutation lock. Batch uses files, each with its read SHA. All-file preflight before writing. snapshot matches old in the original (once, or every occurrence with all=true), refusing overlaps; sequential chains edits. One publication/readback per file. Reply lists every file and before/after SHA: confirmed/refused/in_doubt; partial means mixed confirmed/refused, in_doubt takes precedence. Stops on failure. No auto rollback: reread and edit with fresh versions. Remote host/Windows batch refuses without sending edits.",
