  "schema.tool.purpose.manage_loop": "voluntary attention threads: close/park/reopen/list",
  "schema.tool.0d6f7014305956ba": "Latest lived turns recorded BY CODE, not recalled summaries: arrivals, actual tool calls, outgoing content, decisions not to send and material held by the data-authority check. For an honest account of what just happened. Outside owner scope only the current channel is visible. room chooses ONE place by name/address and returns its turns plus your own note. Observe before deciding to write, especially in an autonomous wake without a current room; reading does not authorize cross-chat disclosure.",
  "schema.tool.3bfc70467bf22d0c": "how many recent turns, 1-20 (default 6)",
  "schema.tool.85964373b176af1e": "name or address of a place; empty means where you are now",
  "schema.tool.purpose.recent_turns": "recent lived turns from actual code records",
  "schema.tool.eb0854449186d579": "The spending agreement with the owner: YOU interpret requests about spending and limits; code counts and displays. “Do not save, dig as deep as needed” -> interpret(mode=free). “Moderate spending” -> interpret(mode=considerate): rebuild background activity (windows, sleep depth) and explain sacrifices. “No more than X per day” -> pledge(daily_tokens/daily_cost): a visible promise with honest reconciliation, not a machine cut-off. “Stop background work” -> interpret(mode=background_paused): finish what is atomic, start no new background work. This does not override Stop or current permissions.",
  "schema.tool.256664ed8e4960c4": "interpret | pledge | status",
