  "schema.tool.ddb68d9644f8e3c9": "Inspect the machine through the configured READ-ONLY observer. overview: CPU, memory, disk, uptime and running commit; containers: activity/restarts, consumption and isolation; ports: exposed ports. Nothing can be restarted or changed here: the observer has no write authority by construction. Useful when a dependency fails, before blaming your code, or when the owner asks about the server. No observer means unavailable evidence, not proof of health.",
  "schema.tool.a111c069f1c996db": "overview | containers | ports | all",
  "schema.tool.purpose.server_status": "configured server observer, read-only",
  "schema.tool.45da75022529814f": "Control only your OWN connected services. list shows available services and quota. restart asks a service to restart via a file signal, not a Docker socket: only listening services (such as mailbot/serverapp) can respond. The external relay process does not take this signal; inspect its available log and tell the owner. Investigate read_log(unit) first; restarting without a cause creates a loop. Restart the agent’s own process through the separate restart_self tool.",
