  "schema.tool.d63dba0344b5f2c2": "Control a durable coding task. start binds a goal to an exact directory and normally creates an isolated Git worktree; target is self or a directory visible to this executor. status/list survive restarts. finish assembles evidence and, for self-code, submits the existing proposal after your own diff review. The root is an address/concurrency boundary, not an override of current permissions. abandon permanently closes the record WITHOUT integration, requires the reason in review and touches neither branch nor worktree. It does not stop processes or release write custody.",
