  "schema.tool.9042535de1e005d4": "Run an arbitrary foreground command at any cwd inside the coding task. Build/test/lint/probe freely; full output becomes durable evidence and the reply is capped. timeout=0 means unbounded. For watchers/servers use coding_process. command is a shell string; for one program with exact arguments use run_command(argv=[...], task_id=...). On Linux local foreground runs, h.read/h.edit/h.write inherit this task and verified command custody; they can edit under their own running command while other writers and Stop still block. Python scripts here can import praxis_hands as h (h.read, h.edit, h.write, h.search): the same version check and write lock as edit; refusals raise. Edit files that way, not with str.replace.",
