  "worker.schema.run_tool.tool": "Run an arbitrary foreground shell command in the task. Full output is retained as evidence; the reply is capped. timeout=0 is unbounded. Use it for tests/builds/lint/probes. Python can import praxis_hands as h (h.read, h.edit, h.write, h.search): the same editor and shared write lock; current local Linux foreground Forge command context is inherited and refusals raise. Edit through those methods, not direct writes after str.replace. Leader exit or a timeout does not prove descendant termination.",
